You can show Francisco that you're the big dog.

173
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:50,640
重点是肢体语言 知道吗
It's all about body language, okay?

174
00:05:50,888 --> 00:05:51,979
向他展示你能领导一切
Show him you can lead the pack.

175
00:05:52,020 --> 00:05:53,220
我来了 老板
Here you go, Boss.

176
00:05:53,278 --> 00:05:54,958
告诉我你最喜欢哪一个 可以吗
Let me know which one you like best, all right?

177
00:05:55,028 --> 00:05:57,858
等我们决定了 会告诉你的
Well, when we decide, we will let you know.

178
00:05:57,918 --> 00:06:00,818
但是首先 我想先来谈谈洗碗机的事儿
But first, I wanted to talk about the, uh -- the dishwasher.

179
00:06:01,338 --> 00:06:02,799
我说了要放在左边
Uh, I wanted it over here on the left,

180
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:04,980
但不知为何 你把它放在右边了
but now, for some reason, it's on the right.

181
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,540
我要你按我要求的把洗碗机放在左边
I would like it on the left like I asked.

182
00:06:07,637 --> 00:06:08,907
听懂我的主张了吗
Asserted?

183
00:06:09,807 --> 00:06:11,257
不不不 眼睛 眼睛看这里 好吗
No, no, no, no. Eyes -- Eyes over here, okay?

184
00:06:11,297 --> 00:06:12,478
这事儿我说了算
This -- This is my thing.

185
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:13,580
给你看个东西
Well, let me show you something.

186
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:14,640
-好 -你看看水池下面
- Yeah. ?- All right, look under the sink.

187
00:06:14,740 --> 00:06:15,380
没问题
Will do.

188
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:17,700
蹲下去 到最下面
Go down. All the way.

189
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:19,720
好了 现在钻到里头去
Okay, now, get in there.

190
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:22,600
抬头看 你看到你左边的管子了吗
Look up. Do you see that post on your left?

191
00:06:22,796 --> 00:06:23,687
等等 好了
Wait. Ho-- Okay.

192
00:06:23,756 --> 00:06:24,447
我无法挪动那玩意儿
I can't move that,

193
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:27,000
所以洗碗机只能放在现在这个位置
which is why the dishwasher needs to stay where it is.

194
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:28,760
还有别的问题吗
Anything else?

195
00:06:29,496 --> 00:06:30,437
没有 我没事
No, I'm good.

196
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:32,420
衣服上沾到了一些木屑
Got some sawdust on your shirt.

197
00:06:33,540 --> 00:06:34,420
很痒啦
It tickles.

198
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:43,340
孩子 醒醒
Hey, kid. Wake up.

199
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:44,320
我们得谈谈
We need to talk.

200
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:45,700
怎么了
What?

201
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:48,960
你妈的车撞了个大坑
Your mom's car got a big dent in it.

202
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:50,680
我知道你当时和她在一起
Now, I know you were with her.

203
00:06:51,140 --> 00:06:52,500
你看到事情经过了吗
Did you see how that happened?

204
00:06:53,674 --> 00:06:56,724
肯定是我们在店里时 有人撞到我们车了
Someone must have hit the car when we were in the store.

205
00:06:56,724 --> 00:06:57,695
那是你老妈说的
That's what your mom said,

206
00:06:57,720 --> 00:07:00,680
但如果有其他原因 比如说...
but if it was something else, like, I don't know,

207
00:07:01,114 --> 00:07:03,823
她出了点小事故 你也可以告诉我啊
she got into a little fender bender, you could tell me.

208
00:07:04,393 --> 00:07:07,373
肯定是我们在店里时 有人撞到我们车了
Someone must have hit the car when we were in the store.

209
00:07:07,473 --> 00:07:08,474
我知道她先跟你通气了 但是...
I know she got to you, but, uh...

210
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:11,160
我要你跟我说实话
I need you to tell me the truth.

211
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:13,540
这冰激凌是给我的吗
Is that ice cream for me?

212
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:14,240
有可能
Could be.

213
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:16,100
你妈的车到底是怎么回事
What happened to your mom's car?

214
00:07:18,620 --> 00:07:20,140
我可以等一整天
I can wait all day,

215
00:07:20,620 --> 00:07:23,200
但是问题是冰激凌是会融化的
but the trouble with ice cream is, it melts.

216
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:24,640
我喜欢融化的冰激凌
I like it when it melts.

217
00:07:24,882 --> 00:07:25,993
什么叫你喜欢融化的冰激凌
What do you mean you like it when it melts?

218
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:27,520
没人喜欢融化的冰激凌
Nobody likes ice cream when it melts.

219
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:28,700
就像汤一样
It's like soup.

220
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:29,640
你讨厌喝汤啊
You hate soup.

221
00:07:29,712 --> 00:07:30,803
不讨厌巧克力汤
Not chocolate soup.

222
00:07:30,852 --> 00:07:32,012
听着 我们都跑题了
Look, we're getting off track here.

223
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:34,620
跟我说说你妈的车到底怎么回事
Tell me what happened to your mom's car,

224
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:35,740
我就把冰激凌给你
and you can have your ice cream.

225
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:37,020
你好啊 杰
Hello, Jay.

226
00:07:37,621 --> 00:07:38,561
歌洛莉亚 我...
Gloria, I...

227
00:07:38,561 --> 00:07:39,132
瞧瞧你
Look at you,

228
00:07:39,380 --> 00:07:41,360
还想贿赂一个五岁的小孩子
trying to bribe a five-year-old.

229
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:42,960
丢死人了你
You should be ashamed.

230
00:07:43,460 --> 00:07:45,220
走吧 乔 既然你醒了
Let's go, Joe. Now that you're awake,

231
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:47,420
妈咪给你弄健康的零食
Mommy's gonna fix you a healthy snack.

232
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,320
查她手机
Check her phone.

233
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:56,240
看她的手机
Check her phone.

234
00:07:56,380 --> 00:07:57,311
把冰激凌留下
And leave the ice cream.

235
00:07:57,840 --> 00:07:59,810
等我回来就刚好全化了
It'll be nice and warm when I get back.

236
00:08:03,899 --> 00:08:05,489
菲尔 你能不能换一下楼下厨房的灯泡
Oh, Phil, could you change the lightbulb down in the kitchen?

237
00:08:05,659 --> 00:08:07,229
你先是让我帮忙清洁纱窗
First you ask me to help clean the window screens.

238
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:09,380
现在让我去做爬梯子和接触电源这种高危工作
Now you want me to do something with a ladder and electricity?

239
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:10,920
你忘记我内裤的事了吗 克莱尔
Have you forgotten about my underwear, Claire?

240
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:13,660
我有些朋友的老公人很差劲
Look, I have friends whose husbands are mean

241
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:15,640
或酗酒 或根本不回家
or drink too much or don't come home at all.

242
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:18,420
然而在那一刻 我羡慕死了那些朋友
And in that moment, I envied those friends.

243
00:08:18,898 --> 00:08:20,948
好吧 我自己去厨房换灯泡
Fine. I will change the lightbulb in the kitchen.

244
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:25,140
你可以把这些柔软蓬松无害的衣服放好
You can put away this nice, soft, fluffy laundry.

245
00:08:25,288 --> 00:08:26,558
-好的 -别担心
- All right. - ?Don't worry.

246
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:28,820
里面连拉链和纽扣都没有
There's not even any zippers or buttons.

247
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:30,120
没有任何尖锐的东西
Nothing sharp in there.

248
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:33,510
我可不想害你出什么叠衣断指意外
Wouldn't want you to lose a finger in a tragic folding incident.

249
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:40,640
我在放好那些安全无害的衣服时
I was putting away that harmless laundry

250
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:42,040
踩到了卢克的滑板
when I stepped on Luke's skateboard,

251
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:44,560
从卸了纱窗的窗口滑了出去 掉到了树篱里
rolled out the screenless window, and landed in the hedge.

252
00:08:44,780 --> 00:08:45,580
不过你说得对
But you're right.

253
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:47,560
我很肯定这跟我的内裤没任何关系
I'm sure it had nothing to do with the underwear.

254
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:49,200
这是自我应验
It's self-fulfilling.

255
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:51,380
菲尔坚信会有坏事发生
Phil believes something bad is gonna happen,

256
00:08:51,380 --> 00:08:53,060
所以他主动让坏事发生
so he makes it happen.

257
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:56,200
被纸割伤了
Ow! Paper cut.

258
00:08:56,220 --> 00:08:57,240
今天当然会这么衰了
Of course, today.

259
00:08:57,880 --> 00:08:58,400
不是吧你
Seriously?

260
00:08:58,796 --> 00:09:00,385
这也是内裤预言的一部分吗
Is this part of the underwear prophecy?

261
00:09:00,555 --> 00:09:02,136
你会不会戏太多了
Aren't you being a little dramatic?

262
00:09:06,175 --> 00:09:07,196
菲尔
Phil?

263
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:09,420
这件事就有点难解释了
Little bit harder to connect the dots on that one.

264
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:11,620
但巧合时有发生嘛
But coincidences do happen.

265
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:13,440
老公 没事的
Honey, it's fine.

266
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:16,180
哪天你接住内裤了 我们再把事办完
We'll just finish our errands on a day when you catch your underwear.

267
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:17,260
演唱会票在你那儿吗
Oh, do you have the tickets?

268
00:09:17,460 --> 00:09:19,480
在车里 但我还是别开车了
They're in the car, but I don't think I should drive.

269
00:09:20,364 --> 00:09:22,184
行吧 但回家你来开
Fine, but you are driving home,

270
00:09:22,274 --> 00:09:24,174
因为今天我要买醉
because today, I'm reelin' in the wine.

271
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:26,780
钥匙在你那儿 抛给我吧
Oh, you've got the keys. Can you toss them to me?

272
00:09:26,864 --> 00:09:28,333
好的 给 不
Yeah, here. No!

273
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:34,540
不 那是我们的钥匙 快停车
No! Those are our keys! Stop!

274
00:09:35,313 --> 00:09:39,643
有人想去看斯迪利·丹乐队 上帝冷笑
Man plans to go to Steely Dan. God laughs.

275
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:42,700
靠 备份钥匙在海莉那里
Damn it. Haley has our other set of keys.

276
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:45,120
对 克莱尔 我真觉得被松鼠咬了
Yes, Claire, I do think it bit me a little!

277
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,380
歌洛莉亚 抱歉
Gloria, I'm sorry.

278
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:49,240
你是我的妻子
You're my wife.

279
00:09:49,620 --> 00:09:51,060
我爱你 信任你
I love you, and I trust you.

280
00:09:51,220 --> 00:09:52,780
跟反社会分子讲道理是行不通的
You can't reason with a sociopath.

281
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:54,540
你得通过示好来诱骗他们
You lure them with kindness.

282
00:09:54,722 --> 00:09:57,481
让他们以为你们在同一阵线
You lull them into thinking you're on the same side,

283
00:09:57,511 --> 00:10:00,781
然后用确凿的证据逮住他们
and then nail them with incontrovertible evidence,

284
00:10:00,871 --> 00:10:02,181
而我已经掌握了证据
which I had.

285
00:10:02,921 --> 00:10:04,911
我还发现 我在她的通讯录里仍然叫
I also found out I'm still listed in her phone

286
00:10:04,961 --> 00:10:07,231
"穿红色运动服的那个杰"
as "Jay, Red Tracksuit."

287
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:10,140
你说你没撞车 我就相信你
If you say you weren't in an accident, I believe you.

288
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:11,220
谢谢老公
Thank you, baby.

289
00:10:12,060 --> 00:10:14,520
不过还有一件事
There is just... one more thing.

290
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:16,620
那是我的手机吗
Is that my phone?

291
00:10:16,620 --> 00:10:18,540
是的 你手机里有很多有趣的照片
Yeah. You've got a lot of interesting pictures here,

292
00:10:18,540 --> 00:10:19,900
但这张尤其有趣
but especially this one.

293
00:10:19,900 --> 00:10:22,100
看起来像是你的车头
It looks like the front end of your car

294
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:24,500
撞上了这辆车的车尾
is rammed into the back end of this car.

295
00:10:24,640 --> 00:10:26,360
我不是什么保险理算员
Now, I'm not an insurance adjuster,

296
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:29,180
但我觉得这可以算是证明
but I would say that that's pretty solid proof

297
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:30,040
你撞了车的铁证啊
you were in an accident.

298
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:31,140
那不是我的车
That's not my car.

299
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:33,460
那你为什么会拍别人车祸的照片呢
But why would you take a picture of some random accident?

300
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:36,100
用来提醒自己生命有多宝贵
To remind me of how precious life is.

301
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:36,960
那是你的车牌号
That's your license plate.

302
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,600
你知道车牌都是什么人做的吗 杰
Do you even know who makes license plates, Jay?

303
00:10:40,340 --> 00:10:40,780
囚犯
Prisoners!

304
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:43,760
你宁愿信一个重刑犯的话
Are you gonna take the word of a convicted felon

305
00:10:43,948 --> 00:10:45,198
也不信你老婆吗
over your wife's?

306
00:10:45,198 --> 00:10:46,728
-毫无道理 -正是
- Makes no sense. - ?Exactly.

307
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:47,720
你到底有什么毛病
What is your problem?!

308
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,580
你看不出这对我有多闹心吗
Don't you see what this is doing to me?!

309
00:10:49,580 --> 00:10:52,180
我得知道你犯错时能承认错误
I need to know that you can admit when you made a mistake.

310
00:10:52,658 --> 00:10:54,448
我知道你心中还有一点善 歌洛莉亚
I know there's good in you, Gloria!

311
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:56,380
给
Here you go.

312
00:10:59,587 --> 00:11:00,648
我... 真是对不起
I -- I am so sorry.

313
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:02,760
好好珍惜它
Cherish this.

314
00:11:02,900 --> 00:11:05,280
这是有手机以来 我首次那么久没碰手机
It was the longest I've been without a phone since phones.

315
00:11:05,620 --> 00:11:08,120
一开始很难适应 大拇指抽搐
It was hard at first -- the twitching thumbs,

316
00:11:08,237 --> 00:11:11,116
总觉得有震动 没被发到朋友圈的沙拉
the phantom vibrations, salads left un-Instagrammed.

317
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:13,460
但之后发生了很奇妙的事
But then the strangest thing happened.

318
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:17,700
你们有停下脚步闻过这些花吗
Have you ever stopped to smell these things?

319
00:11:21,380 --> 00:11:24,600
我好多年都没在现实生活中大笑过了
It's been years since I LOL'd IRL.

320
00:11:25,020 --> 00:11:27,660
我还在车上找到一本旧书 开始读了起来
I even found an old book in the truck and started reading it.

321
00:11:27,940 --> 00:11:29,980
唯一的问题是 总被人打断
The only problem was, people kept interrupting.

322
00:11:34,020 --> 00:11:35,620
我不再需要手机了
I didn't need a phone anymore.

323
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:38,040
我只需要找到安静的地方
I just needed a quiet place to find out

324
00:11:38,040 --> 00:11:39,620
来看他们是如何杀死那只知更鸟的
how they kill that mockingbird.

325
00:11:41,684 --> 00:11:42,515
不好意思
Hey, excuse me.

326
00:11:43,460 --> 00:11:44,440
不好意思
Excuse me!

327
00:11:44,944 --> 00:11:47,774
抱歉打断你抛光 佛朗西斯科[音似旧金山]
S-Sorry to bother you while you sand, Francisco, um --

328
00:11:47,774 --> 00:11:48,884
真有意思
Oh, that's cute.

329
00:11:48,884 --> 00:11:51,274
我想再看一下给橱柜选好的油漆颜色
I just want to revisit the paint color we chose for the cabinets.

330
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:52,580
旧色板你还有吗
Do you still have the old sample?

331
00:11:52,794 --> 00:11:54,523
-也许吧 我去看看 -好的
- Uh, maybe. I'll go look. - ?Okay.

332
00:11:54,623 --> 00:11:56,593
你和老板商量过了吗
Did you discuss this with, uh -- with the boss?

333
00:11:56,773 --> 00:11:58,673
-我不必问... -二爸 大爸在哪儿
- I don't have to discuss it with -- - Daddy, where's Daddy?

334
00:11:58,953 --> 00:11:59,894
你需要什么
Oh. Yeah, what do you need?

335
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:01,280
-我的行李箱 -为什么
- My suitcase. ?- Why?

336
00:12:01,473 --> 00:12:03,513
我要和特里西娅一家去迪士尼
I'm going to Disneyland with Tricia's family.

337
00:12:03,660 --> 00:12:05,020
宝贝女儿 我已经帮你收拾好行李箱了
Sweetie, I already packed your suitcase.

338
00:12:05,983 --> 00:12:07,723
他肯定给我打包了太多鞋
Ugh, there's gonna be too many shoes.

339
00:12:07,723 --> 00:12:09,572
我们几时决定了莉莉可以去迪士尼玩
When did we decide that Lily could go to Disneyland?

340
00:12:09,632 --> 00:12:10,933
我们不是说好要商量这事吗
I thought we were gonna talk about this.

341
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:12,380
她只会缺课一天而已
She's missing one day of school.

342
00:12:12,380 --> 00:12:14,280
我五年级时缺了一半的课 因为被猪咬了
I missed half of the fifth grade because of a pig bite,

343
00:12:14,280 --> 00:12:16,120
而我的教育程度还是和其他人一样啊
and I'm just as educated as anyone else.

344
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:18,880
是吗 我们刚认识时 你以为你在中美洲长大
Really? When we met, you thought you grew up in Central America.

345
